    "turn_text": "Well, first of all, let me just say a thank you to you, Meredith, and to everyone who was listening. Everyone, it results. I'm so delighted that you invited me to be on this call, and because what we're talking about is an incredibly critical issue. You know, in a sense, the grassroots activists and volunteers, you know, we work in circumstances, as you know, where the voices of the rich and powerful are oftentimes the only voices that are heard in Washington, so that the people who are struggling with poverty, with hunger, and those who need to be heard the most are ignored. And that's where you all come in. You really push the political process in an effort to make it respond to those who are least fortunate and the most vulnerable among us. So I'm proud to fight with you. And now we need you more than ever. The majority farm bill passed the House Agriculture Committee in April, totally on a party line vote. Such a partisan bill. And this is my personal view. It's a betrayal. of working families and are most vulnerable. They are going to impose onerous requirements on millions of supplemental nutrition assistance programs to food stamp program recipients.",
