    "turn_text": "a short window of time to make a big difference. So let me just remind you as we get into the rest of the call, kind of what's at stake. Again, the estimates is that 2 million Americans who lose basic food assistance in the house farm bill. Meanwhile, the Senate is on a different track. So all the work we do in in pushing to protect snap and the house side is also going to influence what happens on the Senate side where they're writing their own bipartisan bill and they're definitely paying attention to what happens on the house side. So this is a recess week. So I want to flag first and I that for many of you, this is a key opportunity. Get face to face with your members of Congress. I love Representative Zoloro's suggestion that we also If you can't get them face to face or they're not having a town hall that you go and meet with the local staff and make sure they know what's at stake, you can tailor our talking points for whether it's letters, phone calls with the congressional aid, face to face meetings or town halls to really send a related clear message that we need to protect SNAP. And that means they need to vote no on the House Farm Bill on HR2. So I urge folks to be weighing in on that and just to make sure interesting analysis so we know what's at stake as I mentioned there is. There is some boost to snap benefits. There is some improvement. But as a net, according to Feeding America and the nation's largest network of food banks, we would see a net loss of 9.8 billion meals. That's food not on the tables of folks at risk of going to bed hungry tonight in this house farm bill. So sometimes it's easier to understand what to take when we think about it in the real human side of things. So with that, We're not going to do, we're going to go ahead and skip the chat part though, to be frank, I should have showed that earlier. But we're going to go straight to my colleague, Colin, who's going to lead us, our Director of Communications, who's going to walk us through the process of how we can make the most of this window of opportunity to protect SNAP and the media, which is to focus on our monthly action. Colin, you there? I",
