  {
    "episode_id": 75093,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/5/75093.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 76,
    "turn_text": "This year we set an intention to do outreach in our area and to grow our membership. And we've had results, three outreach events in the first four months of the year. We started with advocacy training for the undoing racism chapter here in Connecticut. They allotted us 45 minutes. We led to a decision on their part to take an action on a results topic at each monthly meeting going forward. Also, we picked up one highly engaged new member, and we averaged 12 people per meeting, most making calls. Then we did advocacy training for two classes at Sacred Hearts University School of Medicine of, excuse me, Public Health, 61 students total an hour and a quarter for each class. That led to an invitation to repeat it there next semester in November. We have three professors attending the IC1 as a real changer. And at least 20 calls went out at the presentation more or more reported later from dorm rooms. We had a new idea to try to set them at ease. We had one professor in each class model how to make the call, even though neither professor had ever called a member of Congress before. Finally, we did a tabling event for a local indivisible group. We had lasers for both domestic and global asks. We generated 36 letters, 27 for domestic in about an hour. And on Thursday, we'll deliver those letters to Representative Jim Himes, who saw us at the event. At all three events, we collected names and info for our action list. And now, Lucinda, we'll talk about the actual presentation.",
