  {
    "episode_id": 75093,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/5/75093.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 83,
    "turn_text": "so I, a couple, a few classmates and I were in a group called the Social Justice Club. And so we're a group of seventh grade students and we meet every other week. And we talk about social issues in our community. And so last year during the club, my dad came in and talked about results and poverty and advocacy. And we all thought that was really interesting. And we all thought that we wanted to do that this year and talk to one of our members of Congress. And we wanted to talk about something that affected us and affected youth. So we chose to do federally funded after school programs. And so during our meetings leading up to the conversation we had with our member of Congress, like my dad came and I just helped, I guess. And we used organizing strategies that I had learned at the conference and through results. And when we were talking in the meeting, we used laser talks that we obviously new from results. And so I guess we use a lot of the advocacy skills that we learned and we did that with a manual cleaver. And when he came into the meeting, he came in with a question for us, which we answered and then we had to get into our topic. And so",
