    "turn_text": "And having been there myself at that meeting, you can see in this picture here that he, you know, he decided to draw a picture of Washington DC for them on the ground. So that's why he's down in his knee and he did a really good job of, you know, explaining that kids have much more of a voice than they think they do because they can influence what their parents do. And he says that you are probably the people that members of Congress are more most scared of. So he told, he definitely encouraged them to keep it up and to keep using their voices. And so it was a great meeting. So thank you, Stella. I appreciate it. So now what we're going to do is we're going to turn it over and switch gears and go to Mia Geisals, our grassroots fundraising manager. And she is going to talk to us about the fundraising campaign that we're, they just started today. So Mia, you can unmute your line and go ahead.",
