    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/5/75093.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 87,
    "turn_text": "Hi, everyone. That is not fair that I have to follow Stella. I'll have to make sure I don't get this spot next time. But thank you very much all. As Joss said, I'm here to talk about the next opportunity to fundraise through results through an online peer-to-peer campaign. So, Joss, if you could go to the next slide, this campaign is called Support Moms Champion Kids, and it's our Spring Friends and Family Fundraising Campaign. Going through the month of May, We have lots of resources available for you. I have a campaign guide with email templates that are ready to use, including talking points about our current work, and ready to use social media posts. We also have some specific resources for first-time fundraisers. And the website is live, so you can go take a look at it at results.salsalabs.org slash moms and kids. And on the next slide, you'll see you might be wondering why we do friends and family campaigns. So if this is new to you, this is a really critical part of our result in your fundraising plan. Grassroots fundraisers bring in about 20% of our unrestricted revenue. And that kind of funding provides for training, resources for volunteers, and staff who support advocates and provide research and expertise on our issues. So it's really quite critical to our overall plan for our work. And then for you on the ground, fundraisers can be a great opportunity to advance the work that you're doing by spreading the word about your work as advocates and to grow your network of supporters. We hear from a lot of people that they've learned about results through friends doing fundraisers or attending an event. It's also an opportunity to have fun. These can be really powerful team building projects. On the next side, you'll see we have really big goals surrounding this campaign. We want to raise $40,000. We also want to meet Joanne's challenge to have 100% of our grassroots groups do some sort of fundraising this year. We're encouraging folks to do this now rather than wait till the fall when we anticipate a more crowded fundraising landscape around the midterm election. So just something to be aware of. If this timeframe works for you, we encourage you to jump in. And the next slide has just a peek at the support mom's champion kids fundraising page so you can get a sense of what they look like. This one was set up by her own Lisa Marshall who is participating in the campaign. The two stars highlight really great aspects of the page. One is that she set a goal of $300 and you can see on her thermometer she's a third of the way there. She's also included just a brief description of her personal story and why fundraising for results is important to her. along with a really happy photo. So just to give you a sense of what these look like, they're very simple pages and the templates are all there. So nothing, you don't have to have any web development skills to set up your fundraising page. And then the next slide, just a few next steps. So if you're planning to join or want to learn more, please Join us this Thursday on the kickoff campaign. So this is a training webinar, a really good thing to join, especially if you're new to fundraising. You can go ahead and get started at results.salsalabs.org slash moms and kids. The website is also up on our website at results.org. So you can find it there. And then please be in touch if you have any questions. My email is on the slide and is also in some of the weekly updates and the Note that Joss sent out earlier, so I would encourage you to please get in touch. I can always walk you through these things one on one. And thank you so much to those who have already started fundraising and joined the campaign. We are on our way to hitting that big goal.",
