    "turn_idx": 92,
    "turn_text": "Wonderful. First, I'd like to just thank everyone for just the positive support and feedback when I worked with our anti-oppression council and our work that we've been doing across the organization. And so I'm really proud and excited for what's to come and all the things that's going on. So I definitely wanted to mention that to everyone. Next, we have our upcoming grassroots board member seat, which will be vacant. We've had Beth Wilson to serve two full tiles who have done an awesome magnificent job and representing our grassroots and being a strong voice and making sure we're being heard on the board. And so her seat is vacant and we are looking to find someone who will be interested in either nominating themselves or someone else who they know would like to be a voice on our board of directors to serve in that seat. nominations are now open and will end on Sunday. On Monday, May 14th, I think I have the date right, is Monday May 14th, correct? So nominations will end. On Monday May 14th, please nominate someone or yourself who you believe will be a strong voice to represent our graduates here on the board. And last, before I have the opportunity, I would like to just say thank you to Christy Martino for her wonderful service and time and results. I don't know if everyone is aware, but Christy will be leaving results soon. And so I just want to personally thank Christy for the hard work, the dedication, the love, the support, being a strong voice. Not only for results in the organization, but even through our experts, cold hurt, and all the other organizations she's done. Christy, we love you, and we will miss you nearly. Again, thank you for just your service, and we definitely look forward to just seeing you. Good thing you could be a strong voice for our community. Thank you.",
