    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/5/75093.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 93,
    "turn_text": "Thank you, Maxine. This is Christy. That's not fair to do when I have some announcements to make, and I'm all choked up. Thank you so much, and I have so much love for you as well. So, on that note, I have a, I get to be the friendly reminder that the IC is coming up. Please join us. It's such an amazing experience to be together with everyone. You know, you're in Washington, DC. Now is the time to do something. It really does reflect that you're not alone. The Early Bird Registration Deadline is May 15. That's only two weeks away. So take advantage of that when you can. And then a couple of other things coming up in the near future. We have the House and Center on recess. Our next US Poverty Free Agent call is Tuesday, May 15th at 1 PM and 8 PM. We have our next anti-oppression training webinar coming up on Tuesday, May 15th, which will have a really exciting activities to do. We'll do some cultural sketches to understand how our identities influence our values. So please join us for that. And you can find all of those events on our results events calendar. So I do want to say that Maxine mentioned it. I do have a bit of personal news. This will be my last national webinar as a staff member at results. I'm moving on to my next adventure at the end of the month. But I will be back as a volunteer, of course. But I did want to just say really quickly that my experience working with my incredible colleagues, my forever friends and the experts on poverty cohort, and all of you has been the most transformative period of my life thus far, truly. And when I first started working at results, my friends and family, you know, folks that have known me forever said, what happened to you? It's like, You lost your bitter cynicism or something. And I did. And that's because of you. Because of you all, I found a way to be hopeful, a way to keep going and keep fighting. And I cannot thank you enough for that. And once an organizer, always an organizer. So the best way for me to say goodbye is to make an ask. So on to the final action for tonight. How about before we go to bed, we hit submit on that letter to the editor. Speak up, speak out, let your community and your representatives know that we're not gonna stand by to watch food taken off the tables of Americans. Let's protect SNAP, let's keep fighting, and thank you all again for being my inspiration always. And Joss, maybe if you wanna open up the lines, we can cheer each other on, and I can say goodbye one last time to you all.",
